{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for contract amendment 2 at exact head b9fded01cb688a5f91d56b4b60373b6faeb72d18, resting on all 8 artifacts.\n\nP1 — Founding must authorize the canonical repository, not just the first admin key (docs/protocol.md R-GEN-10, R-API-3, open point 33; packages/contract/src/transports.ts RoomDraft/Founding). Both founding routes are unauthenticated and repo is selected by the caller. The required checks prove only that the founder controls its newly chosen admin key. No rule proves that it may import or publish to that repository. Yet R-PUB-3 subsequently has the deployment mint a canonical write token. A caller can therefore nominate someone else's repository accessible to the deployment and install its own first admin and recovery key. This is an authorization gap in the specified integration, not a claim that the current memory-only Room ports have already exploited a live repository. General optional Access/rate limiting does not decide authority over an individual repo. Require an owner/operator-authorized onboarding binding or allocate a fresh isolated canonical repo for public founding. Reject unauthorized existing repositories before reading canonical contents, minting credentials, sealing entries or binding names. Bind any authorization to the canonical repository identity and signed genesis, and recheck it at found rather than trusting editable draft fields. Add normative unauthorized-existing-repo, altered-repo-after-draft, authorized-import and isolated-public-creation cases; list the required lane/integration edits.\n\nP1 — Serialize the repository-to-room binding (R-GEN-10/11, R-PUB-1). Name uniqueness is insufficient. Two valid signed founding bodies with different names and room keys may name the same canonical repository, and both satisfy every new rule. Each gets its own first admin, recovery path, sequencer, log publisher and publication slot. A compromised or independently administered second room can then bypass the first room's governance; separate slots also break the promised single publication authority and compete for refs/artroom/log. The plan specifies one Room sequencer per repository. Require one authoritative Room binding per canonical repository identity, atomically allocated during authorized founding and retained through incomplete-founding retries, analogous to the name binding. Same-genesis retry must complete forward; a different genesis for an already bound repo must fail without acquiring canonical publication authority. Test simultaneous founding under different names for the same repo, duplicate imports, canonical-name aliases and recovery after binding but before genesis sealing. Explicit room succession, if needed, should be a separate authorized operation, not arbitrary second founding.\n\nAdditional clarification requested: state the pinned policy used for queued notify replay in R-LOG-10/13, and include activation between queueing and notification sealing as a normative case. Lane A stores the original queue policy; lane L currently rejects it because it compares against the later active policy. The log verdict records that concrete failure. Also explicitly distinguish bearer authentication expiry/revocation from R-IDEM-2's signed-envelope replay promise: R-CRED-10 authenticates the bearer before constructing an envelope, so a revoked bearer cannot retrieve a lost receipt through bearerAct even though a retained signed envelope can return its original result after key revocation. A short rule and acceptance case will prevent implementations from making contradictory retry claims.\n\nValidation: reviewed all changed protocol sections and all 8 artifacts, including the new lifecycle example and type exports. Candidate root typecheck passed. Existing policy suite passed 189 tests on Node and 188 in workerd (one Node-only compiler test skipped there). Independent compile checks accepted bearer propose/reclaim reasons, MCP structured not-found and checker activation digests, while rejecting bearer roster/actor injection, bearer session requests, null MCP explanation, nonzero premature reopened count and treating raw byte streams as decoded updates. These diagnostics were confined to the detached review worktree. No deployed repository, token or service was touched.\n\nArchitecture: the five documented integration corrections are sound: immutable name binding, repeated genesis validation, pre-upgrade WebSocket authentication, RPC byte decoding, and preserving because. Later recompute/land-evaluation events fit the acyclic log. Repository onboarding and a single canonical Room authority must now be made equally explicit.\n\nSecurity: signed genesis proves key possession; it does not authorize the deployment to act on a chosen repository. The two founding findings are required before a real Artifacts adapter is connected. Bearer kind restrictions, fragment-only invitation secrets and token subprotocol handling are otherwise clear.\n\nSimplification: keep one repository onboarding binding as the source of room identity and publication authority; derive the convenience name binding from it. The documented no-Git-signature decision is sound with signed checkpoints, signed entries and content digests. State re-derivation is explicitly left open with a reason as condition 7 allows; that is a stated limitation rather than completed full-platform verification. The lane edit map is useful and should include the repository authorization/binding repairs.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b06139fa0f0695c778e197fd4ac75053d9af1071","binding":"assigned","head":"b9fded01cb688a5f91d56b4b60373b6faeb72d18","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:34bef21b6810813b04293122a237f24d368880b3\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bf17b0654beb0b883f5c4f9b22ba4aa1d2e692fd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:893cbcc6942862cb0fe016815a978d39ad63ceff","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}